# Raw browser captures and debug artifacts — these carry LIVE credentials
# (session cookies, bearer JWTs, access_token query params) and must never be
# committed. Keep them local only.
#
# data/ is where they all live now, and it is ignored WHOLESALE rather than by
# extension: everything dropped in there is credential-grade by assumption, so
# a capture saved with an unanticipated name (a .txt frame dump, a .flow from
# mitmproxy, a saved response body) is covered without anyone having to
# remember to add a pattern first. The per-extension rules below stay as a
# safety net for a capture saved outside data/ by accident.
data/
*.har
*.log.jsonl
request-curl.sh
.juggler/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# uv-managed dev virtualenv (the tooling "workshop"; never the shipped proxy)
.venv/

# Live credentials for manual testing -- never commit these
.refresh_token
*.token
.cache_encryption_key
.refresh_token_key
.refresh_token_value
.encryption_key
.encryption_value
m365_credentials.json
m365_openai_proxy.json

# The proxy's four plain-text credential files (any --credentials-prefix,
# not just the default "m365_openai_proxy") -- never commit these, they
# hold either a live refresh token or the encrypted-cache equivalent
*.refresh_token.conf
*.encrypted_refresh_token.conf
*.cache_encryption_key.conf
*.local_storage_key.conf

# Proxy's own runtime log -- never commit (should never contain secrets by
# design, but treat it as sensitive operational data regardless)
m365_openai_proxy.log
